  description: Radium is a chemical element with symbol Ra and atomic number 88.
    It is the sixth element in group 2 of the periodic table, also known as the alkaline
    earth metals. Pure radium is almost colorless, but it readily combines with nitrogen
    (rather than oxygen) on exposure to air, forming a black surface layer of radium
    nitride (Ra3N2).
